WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.644
With Flask-Babel, you
write gettext calls,

2
00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:06.674
and translators fill
each extracted PO file.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.215
Babel does its part
well: it formats dates,

4
00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:13.326
numbers, and currencies
from CLDR data.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.144
General Translation fills Babel's
PO files for every language,

6
00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:19.780
so you keep Flask-Babel.

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.008
Keep an English catalog current,

8
00:00:23.008 --> 00:00:24.992
and point the gt config at it.

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.816
Then npx gt translate fills every
language before pybabel compile

10
00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:32.000
runs in CI.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.798
A Glossary keeps terms consistent,

12
00:00:34.798 --> 00:00:37.502
and reviewers can edit each
entry in the Dashboard.

13
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.808
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
